@namespace FamilyHQ.WebUi.Components.Dashboard

@* One phone notification. data-ping-at/data-event-id/data-is-default let both the E2E suite and the
   preprod smoke suite address a row by what it IS rather than by its position in the list — pings
   reorder as time passes, so a positional selector would silently drift to the wrong row. *@
<div class="reminder-ping-row"
     data-testid="reminder-ping-row"
     data-ping-at="@Ping.TriggerAt.ToString("O")"
     data-event-id="@Ping.EventId"
     data-is-default="@(Ping.IsDefault ? "true" : "false")"
     @onclick="() => OnOpenEvent.InvokeAsync(Ping.EventId)">
    <span class="reminder-ping-row__time">@Ping.TriggerAt.ToString("HH:mm")</span>
    <span class="reminder-ping-row__icon" aria-hidden="true">@ReminderRowDisplay.MethodIcon(Ping.Method)</span>
    <div class="reminder-ping-row__body">
        <span class="reminder-ping-row__title">@Ping.EventTitle</span>
        <span class="reminder-ping-row__detail">
            @ReminderRowDisplay.Lead(Ping.Minutes, Ping.EventIsAllDay) · @ReminderRowDisplay.StartsAt(Ping.EventStart, Ping.EventIsAllDay)
        </span>
    </div>
    @if (Ping.IsDefault)
    {
        <span class="reminder-ping-row__default-tag" data-testid="reminder-ping-default-tag">default</span>
    }
    @* The server substitutes the owning calendar's name as a member when it can resolve one, so an
       empty Members list means it could not — there is no calendar name anywhere to fall back to,
       not just none wired to this view. Rendering nothing here is the honest answer; inventing a
       placeholder ("this calendar") would assert something meaningless to a family reading a wall
       display, which is worse than admitting the gap — the same reasoning behind the standing
       all-day footnote below. *@
    <div class="reminder-ping-row__people">
        @foreach (var member in Ping.Members)
        {
            <span @key="member.DisplayName"
                  class="reminder-member-chip"
                  style="--chip-color: @(member.Color ?? "var(--theme-accent)")">@member.DisplayName</span>
        }
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The ping this row renders. Required — there is no meaningful empty row.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public UpcomingReminderViewModel Ping { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>Raised with the event's id when the row is tapped. The whole row is the tap target.</summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<Guid> OnOpenEvent { get; set; }
}
